id: design.rate-limiting
kind: design
title: Rate limiting
aliases: rate limit, throttling, 429, token bucket
tags: api, reliability, security
questions:
  - how would you rate-limit an API?
invariant: Requests are admitted against a budget per identity and window, with a defined response when the budget is exhausted.
answer_30s: Apply a per-identity budget (token bucket or sliding window) close to the entry point, count it centrally, and return 429 with Retry-After plus limits in headers.
answer_2m: |
  Decisions to state explicitly: the identity (api key, user, tenant, IP -- per
  IP is weak behind NAT, per user is what customers experience), the algorithm
  (token bucket for burst tolerance, sliding window for accuracy, fixed window
  for simplicity), where it executes (a shared store like Redis, or a local
  limiter per replica which is cheaper but approximate), and what happens on
  exceed (reject with 429 and Retry-After, or queue, or degrade). Rate limiting
  is distinct from load shedding: it protects fairness between clients, shedding
  protects the service itself, and a good system does both -- with a global
  concurrency limit behind per-tenant quotas. The distributed counter is the
  hard part: it must be atomic, fast, and bounded in cardinality.
when_to_use:
  - public or partner APIs, expensive endpoints, per-tenant fairness
avoid_when:
  - as a substitute for overload protection (per-client limits do not bound total concurrency)
commands:
  - kubectl get ingress -A => where a peripheral rate limit is configured (annotations/waf)
failure_modes:
  - per-replica counters, so the effective limit is replicas times the configured value
  - no Retry-After header, so well-behaved clients hammer at full speed
  - limiting by IP behind a shared NAT, punishing innocent tenants
follow_ups:
  - how do you rate limit across many replicas?
related:
  - design.load-shedding
  - design.redis-cache
  - design.distributed-locking
  - rust.tower
  - recipe.rate-limited-api
sources:
  - https://cloud.google.com/architecture/rate-limiting-strategies-techniques
